+// blocking=true (the pre-M9 behaviour) when queue_type is not in_order, since
+// only an in-order queue lets the eventual GEMM kernels rely on program order
+// for correctness while the wait below exists solely to recycle staging
+// (moe_3gemm_swiglu_opt.cpp callers still see one call, one function).
+// staging is only touched on the async (in_order) path.
